<figure class="pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title" aria-describedby="pipeline-description">
  <figcaption>
    <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge distillation</p>
    <h2 id="pipeline-title">One position. Two paths.</h2>
    <p id="pipeline-description">The teacher supplies a target evaluation. The compact student learns to approximate it from the same position.</p>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="pipeline-grid">
    <article class="pipeline-card source-card">
      <span class="step">01 · Source</span>
      <h3>Chess position</h3>
      <div class="source-board" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <code>rnbqkbnr/<br />pppppppp/<br />8/8/8/8/<br />PPPPPPPP/<br />RNBQKBNR</code>
      <p>FEN stores a complete board state in one compact string.</p>
    </article>

    <div class="pipeline-paths">
      <article class="pipeline-card teacher-card">
        <span class="path-label">Teacher path</span>
        <span class="step">02A · Label</span>
        <h3>LC0 evaluates</h3>
        <p>Ten seconds of engine analysis produces the target score.</p>
        <strong>+84 <small>centipawns</small></strong>
      </article>
      <article class="pipeline-card student-card">
        <span class="path-label">Student path</span>
        <span class="step">02B · Learn</span>
        <h3>8 × 8 × 7 tensor</h3>
        <p>Piece type, colour, and location pass through a compact model.</p>
        <strong>+71 <small>centipawns</small></strong>
      </article>
    </div>

    <article class="pipeline-card compare-card">
      <span class="step">03 · Compare</span>
      <h3>L1 error</h3>
      <p>The absolute difference trains the student.</p>
      <strong>|84 − 71|</strong>
      <span class="error-value">13 cp</span>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="pipeline-note">Repeated across <strong>15,000 positions</strong> and <strong>nine student architectures</strong>. Scores shown here are illustrative.</p>
</figure>

